-- title:
--   Distinct minimal primes over p together with 1/j generate everything
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero modulus $M$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ which contains the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$, in the form: every unit $u$ of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ with `ZMod.unitsMap` image $1$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ lies in $H$. Assume the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` $= q^{-1}\cdot(\text{the integral } j\text{-numerator power series over }\mathbb{Q})$ lies in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the integral form ratios for the full modular group; write $F$ for `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓM M H)`, the corresponding field for the subgroup `ΓM M H` of $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$, and $j \in F$ for the element with underlying series `jqModC ℚ`. The ring in play is `chartAlgInf p (ΓM M H) hj`, the subalgebra of $F$ consisting of the elements integral over the subalgebra of $F$ generated by $j^{-1}$ over the base ring `R p`. Let $P$ and $P'$ be two distinct ideals of this ring, each a minimal prime over the ideal generated by the image of the natural number $p$. Then $P \sqcup P' \sqcup (j^{-1}) = \top$, the span being of the element `jInvChartInf` $= j^{-1}$ of the ring.
--
--   This is the statement that each cusp of $X_H(M)$ in characteristic $p$ lies on only one of the two irreducible components of the reduction, the components meeting only at supersingular points (Deligne–Rapoport VI.6.9, Katz–Mazur 13.4.7), expressed as a comaximality statement for two distinct minimal primes over $p$ in the chart at infinity together with $1/j$. It feeds the analysis of the crossings of the two charts of the integral two-chart model of $X_H(M)$ at $p$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XHDRLevel_sup_sup_span_jInvChartInf_eq_top_of_mem_minimalPrimes_gammaH.lean

